{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Orxta","id":"343605682580488215","is_bot":0,"username":"robdor."},"author_id":"343605682580488215","channel_id":"746965729420509185","content":"I think the javelin crossbow sounds pretty balanced as-is. You say a lvl 20 fighter could do \"8d10+4d6+60 or roughly 118 dmg a round\". However, a normal fighter with those feats could do 4d10+60 or 82 damage per round. And there's one more drawback that hasn't been mentioned. Ranged weapons use dex. The lvl 20 fighter in question would have to pump strength to 16, and still have a dex of 20 to get that damage. Realistically, this will be used by a strength based fighter, not a dex fighter. So you can chip off 3-5 damage shot. It's still good, but not getting to use dex for the extra damage is kind of like subtracting a d8 from the roll.\n\nIt would be really cool if they had to roll a con save or be pushed back 5ft. \nI imagine that the bonus action is setting up a tripod with a swivel.","created_at":"2021-05-29T05:38:20.882000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"848072753575624704","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
